{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00717",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.42,
      "end_seconds": 13.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. It's my eyes, the contact lenses, they've gone uncomfortable. I forgot to say on the phone, I wear them every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.64,
      "end_seconds": 17.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "What does uncomfortable mean?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.49,
      "end_seconds": 32.22,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "Dry, and sort of scratchy by the afternoon. I have to take them out by about four, and my eyes feel tired."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.2,
      "end_seconds": 39.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "How long have you worn contact lenses? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.44,
      "end_seconds": 53.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.41,
      "text": "Eight years, but it's only got bad recently. I'm forgetting how long. Since March, I think? Or April. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.9,
      "end_seconds": 61.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "That's fine. What are you putting in your eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.83,
      "end_seconds": 71.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Lubricating drops, four times a day. Hypromellose, I think the packet says. Does that sound right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.1,
      "end_seconds": 80.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "That's right. And the other tablets you mentioned on the form?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.3,
      "end_seconds": 89.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Cetirizine, 10 mg once a day, for my hay fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.03,
      "end_seconds": 101.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Good. How many hours a day are you in lenses, and where, a screen, air conditioning? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.19,
      "end_seconds": 111.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Ten, eleven hours. I'm at a computer all day, in an air-conditioned office. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.45,
      "end_seconds": 123.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "That's the classic recipe for dry eyes. How do you clean and store the lenses? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.04,
      "end_seconds": 134.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "I use the solution, and I change the case every month. Or every two months. Sometimes three. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.93,
      "end_seconds": 144.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "That's a little long, the case should be changed monthly. And do you ever sleep in them? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.66,
      "end_seconds": 150.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Once or twice, if I'm tired. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.98,
      "end_seconds": 157.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Please try not to, that raises the risk of infection. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.15,
      "end_seconds": 161.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "I'll try. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.91,
      "end_seconds": 172.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Let me have a look at your eyes. Chin on the rest. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.99,
      "end_seconds": 196.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.4,
      "end_seconds": 210.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "Fine. There's no infection and nothing is scratched. Your eyes are a little dry on the surface. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.12,
      "end_seconds": 216.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "So it's not serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.62,
      "end_seconds": 229.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Not serious. I'd say it's dry eye related to your lens wear, made worse by the screen and the air conditioning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.22,
      "end_seconds": 234.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "What do I do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.32,
      "end_seconds": 249.04,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "Wear glasses on some days to give your eyes a rest, take the lenses out by the time you get home, and use preservative-free drops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.57,
      "end_seconds": 255.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "The drops I've got, are they preservative-free? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.62,
      "end_seconds": 266.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Not the ones you've got, ask the pharmacist for single-use vials, and keep using them. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.77,
      "end_seconds": 272.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Right, that's useful. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.61,
      "end_seconds": 281.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Blink fully when you're at the screen, and look away every twenty minutes, twenty seconds."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.23,
      "end_seconds": 288.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I will, I'll set an alarm. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.61,
      "end_seconds": 299.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.15,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, to see if the lenses are more comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.88,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Six weeks. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
